eam: structurally append-only but causally incoherent. The ","school":"school-0"},{"addressed_problem_refs":["question-2da717017468d2da3c501dd1dc4ce3cd"],"artifact_ref":"87d12bb19f2ba65ca786dc0c6a45cba830eadbe1cc79f2369aa3bb4fdd1d8b61","citation_id":"87d12bb19f2b","claim":"Adjudication between rival criteria: the 'last complete event' criterion and the 'causal fingerprint' criterion are both necessary but neither is sufficient alone. The correct criterion is their conjunction: resumption is safe iff (1) the last event is well-formed and complete, AND (2) the causal fingerprint matches, AND (3) no intermediate event declares logical incompleteness (e.g., a 'begin' without a matching 'commit'). This conjunction subsumes both rivals and adds a logical-unit integrity check.","lineage":{"dependence_refs":[],"evidence_refs":[],"mention_refs":["ba687c5f145e404c53a84549cf366e0b6e0106eec67404c07231357fed09e672","30be11905db881ea7a4e488a8e68f34e4f6b262380bb3b1a31ceb9763a9aea81","8929789f0ae19d5b1c2537f758719daf17f9908ce1fb0ca3fa0cc60fe9f2a2a3"],"source_refs":[],"trace_refs":[],"warrant_refs":[]},"mechanism":"The 'last complete event' criterion ensures structural integrity of the log. The 'causal fingerprint' criterion ensures causal identity continuity. The 'logical-unit integrity' criterion ensures semantic coherence: multi-event units must be complete or explicitly aborted. Token-budget exhaustion can violate any of the three independently: mid-write (violates 1), model update (violates 2), mid-inference-step (violates 3). Since each violation independently corrupts a different aspect of identity, all three must hold. The mechanism is a three-stage gate: structural check, fingerprint check, logical-unit check.","overturn_conditions":[],"rendered_text":"[87d12bb19f2b] (school: school-0)\nCLAIM: Adjudication between rival criteria: the 'last complete event' criterion and the 'causal fingerprint' criterion are both necessary but neither is sufficient alone. The correct criteri